  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "A component's identity is minted from any `{expression}` in its markup (omega-svelte emits no per-file fact), so a component whose markup contains no single-identifier expression is not registered under its own name and a `renders` edge naming it has no `declares` edge to a file.",
      "`<Foo/>` is resolved to a file by Svelte's filename convention (`svelte:component-name:{path.stem}`), not by the import: omega-javascript spans `import.module` on the specifier string and the local binding on a sibling node, so neither a span join nor a field join relates the two. Two `Button.svelte` files in different directories therefore both claim the name.",
      "`{...}` is one raw JS/TS token in the Svelte grammar, so an expression is stated only when it is a single identifier: `{$page.url}`, `onclick={() => ...}` and `use:clickOutside={opts}` contribute no handler or store name.",
      "Runes in `.svelte.js` / `.svelte.ts` rune modules are outside the `**/*.svelte` glob that makes `svelte:component:{path}` meaningful, so they are not stated.",
      "Runtime-generated component trees, `<svelte:component this={X}>` and reactive scheduling remain runtime ceilings."
    ]
  },
